Checkout has to fail closed — a member with too many books out, or an unpaid fine, shouldn't walk out with another one:

```java
class Member {
    List<Loan> activeLoans;
    double outstandingFines;
    int borrowLimit;

    Loan checkout(BookItem item) {
        if (item.status != BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE)
            throw new IllegalStateException("item not available");
        if (activeLoans.size() >= borrowLimit)
            throw new BorrowLimitExceededException();
        if (outstandingFines > MAX_ALLOWED_FINE)
            throw new UnpaidFineException();

        item.status = BookItemStatus.CHECKED_OUT;
        Loan loan = new Loan(this, item, LocalDate.now());
        activeLoans.add(loan);
        return loan;
    }
}
```

Order matters: check availability first so a blocked member gets a clear "not available" instead of a confusing borrow-limit error on a book they couldn't have taken anyway.

```java
class BookItem {
    BookItemStatus status;
    Book book;

    void returnItem() {
        Reservation next = book.nextWaitingReservation();
        if (next != null) {
            status = BookItemStatus.ON_HOLD;
            next.markReady(this, Duration.ofHours(48));
        } else {
            status = BookItemStatus.AVAILABLE;
        }
    }
}

class Reservation {
    void markReady(BookItem item, Duration expiry) {
        this.status = ReservationStatus.READY;
        this.assignedItem = item;
        this.expiresAt = Instant.now().plus(expiry);
        notificationService.notify(this.member, item);
    }
}
```

If `markReady`'s expiry elapses unclaimed, a scheduled job flips the reservation to `EXPIRED`, calls `returnItem()` again to offer the copy to the next person in line, and repeats.
